From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:18:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: advertise VK_KHR_pipeline_binary

VP_ANDROID_17_requirements makes this extension mandatory. It lets an
application take the compiled form of a pipeline out of the implementation,
keep it, and hand it back to create the same pipeline without recompiling.

This driver builds its pipelines out of the common runtime's shader objects,
so the common runtime already has everything a binary needs: it serializes a
shader into a binary, reconstructs one from binary data, and answers the
pipeline key. None of its five entrypoints is overridden here, which leaves
only the capabilities to declare.

The properties say what this driver does not have. There is no cache of its
own behind the application's, so there is no internal cache to report, to
control, or to prefer, and nothing is precompiled into one; a binary's bytes
are the serialized shader rather than a compressed form of it. An application
that asks for a binary from a pipeline creation info alone is therefore told
the binary is missing, which the extension allows for any reason, and gets its
binaries from a created pipeline instead.

Metal's own MTLBinaryArchive is deliberately not used for this. It is keyed by
the pipeline descriptors this driver builds internally rather than by anything
the application names, and it serializes only as a whole archive to a file
URL, so it can neither produce one binary per shader nor return a binary's
bytes, which is what this extension trades in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index d63f71d45122df8396c2e5044fe140b56c704619..52114fe03f98bd24c4e8d18760f8275cacf293d7 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@ kk_get_device_extensions(const struct kk_instance *instance,
       .KHR_index_type_uint8 = true,
       .KHR_load_store_op_none = true,
       .KHR_maintenance5 = true,
+      .KHR_pipeline_binary = true,
       .KHR_maintenance6 = true,
       .KHR_map_memory2 = true,
       .KHR_push_descriptor = true,
@@ -499,6 +500,9 @@ kk_get_device_features(
       /* VK_EXT_device_address_binding_report */
       .reportAddressBinding = true,
 
+      /* VK_KHR_pipeline_binary */
+      .pipelineBinaries = true,
+
       /* VK_EXT_image_compression_control and its swapchain companion.
        * Metal never tells the driver whether it compressed a texture and
        * offers no fixed-rate control, so every query answers "no
@@ -833,6 +837,19 @@ kk_get_device_properties(const struct kk_physical_device *pdev,
       /* VK_KHR_line_rasterization */
       .lineSubPixelPrecisionBits = 8,
 
+      /* VK_KHR_pipeline_binary.
+       *
+       * The common runtime serves a binary out of the shader it was made
+       * from, and this driver keeps no cache of its own behind the
+       * application's, so there is no internal cache to report, control or
+       * prefer, nothing is precompiled into one, and a binary's bytes are
+       * the serialized shader rather than a compressed form of it. */
+      .pipelineBinaryInternalCache = false,
+      .pipelineBinaryInternalCacheControl = false,
+      .pipelineBinaryPrefersInternalCache = false,
+      .pipelineBinaryPrecompiledInternalCache = false,
+      .pipelineBinaryCompressedData = false,
+
       /* VK_KHR_maintenance5 */
       .earlyFragmentMultisampleCoverageAfterSampleCounting = true,
       /* A pipeline whose static sample mask discards samples counts them in
